Z||000000||fiero87||02-20-2001||12:52 AM||||Looking for some info...<P>I'm in need of a new 2.8 for my 86 GT.  And i was looking through my local classifieds and somone was advertising a recently rebuilt 2.8 from an 87 S-10 pickup.  I know both are RWD, so does this mean all i would have to change is the intake?  i can still use all the stock sensors and bolt ons?  Are there any hp and tq differences between the  two engines?  Any info would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||02-20-2001||07:29 AM||||I'm not sure but I think the S-10 engine does not have the same big valve heads as the Fiero.  Also the timing chain cover/oil pan may be different.  Fieros have a unique water pump.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrossum||02-20-2001||09:20 AM||||s-10 engine will noy work. even though the fiero is rear wheel drive, the engine and trans are front wheel drive units. the engine mounts are in the wrong spot on the  s-10 engine.||||reg||11
Z||000003||Formula88||02-20-2001||01:18 PM||||Actually it would work, but at a cost.  It'd be the same amount of work as installing a 3.4 out of a F-body, since they're both RWD.  You'd be better off doing the 3.4 conversion.  If you want a bolt-in swap, you have to go with a FWD engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||02-20-2001||05:35 PM||||Starter is on the wrong side too. You need to find a 'W' block out of a FWD car.||||reg||1
